{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And she went down to the spring and filled her pitcher and came up.</b> It does not say ותשאב — 'and she drew' — as it says the second time: ותשאב לכל גמליו — 'and she drew for all his camels.' From here the Rabbis of blessed memory derived: ״ותמלא כדה ותעל״ — all the other women go down and fill from the spring, but this one — as soon as the waters saw her, they rose toward her. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to her: You are a sign for your children. And this is what is written immediately afterward: ״וירץ העבד לקראתה״ — for the waters had risen toward her." "<b>And you should be roused</b> to understand that there was inscribed here this first Name of the Name of seventy-two letters (ע״ב), which acts upon the waters drawn from the twenty-six (כ״ו), and by this power the waters rose toward her, and it was a sign for her children that the sea would be split for them and that the well would rise toward them by its power. For the splitting of the sea and the waters from the rock were by means of the staff of Moses, in which was engraved the Name of seventy-two letters (ע״ב אותיות)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:43.652489179Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}